# Club & Grub level file - format 2 (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md 7.11). Versus arena #1 of docs/expansion/DESIGN.md E.5:
# Totem Ring - jungle, the edges joined left-right, a carved totem in the middle with the cookpot on its top, bridges
# either side 3 rows over the floor, springs up to the wrap ledge that runs across the seam. Owner: DA (arenas,
# docs/expansion/PLAN.md 6.1). Rules: docs/LEVEL_DESIGN.md 15.8. Dressing: art-B's hand-over
# (.tools/asset_candidates/expansion/_handover/ARENA_TOTEM_RING.md).
#
# Layout notes (the E.5 sketch, plus what the sketch leaves open; proven by a scripted match, see the end):
# - Tiers: floor (row 10), bridges (row 7) and totem top (row 4) are 3 rows apart; the wrap ledge (row 5) is 2 rows
#   over a bridge end and 5 over the floor: from the floor only the springs (cols 1 and 18, -224 = 105 px) reach it.
# - Springs one cell further out than in the sketch (cols 1 / 18, still under the wrap ledge): every strike ends with
#   a hop (3 px forward, 6 px low, a 15 px pogo off a spot) and a hero coming down from it within about 20 px of a
#   spring is thrown 105 px up. In the sketch the stands of both floor spots (cols 3 / 16) lay in a spring's reach;
#   now no spot stand and no spawn does. The floor spots moved one cell inward with them (cols 4 / 15).
# - Spots (visible, refill 15 s after they are emptied): the two floor spots (cols 4 / 15), two in the totem faces -
#   (9, 5) at head height from the left bridge, (10, 7) level with the right bridge (low strike) - and the big spot in
#   the totem's base (9, 9), struck with a forward strike from either floor half. The hit test reaches one column past
#   the club (PHYSICS 8.3), and the totem is two cells wide, so each totem spot is also struck from the other side.
#   The big spot's giant falls 7 rows onto the totem top beside the signature cookpot: dig on the floor, collect on
#   top. Food knocked out of a floor spot under a bridge arcs up and mostly lands on that bridge.
#   (Phase 2: at G1 the big spot lay in the right floor under spawn 1's feet; core-B's V4.b set measured spawn 1
#   winning 58-60 % of 48 Grub Stack rounds. In the totem's base it is the same walk from both floor spawns, and its
#   giant lands where all four spawns are one or two jumps away; the set is within +/-15 points now.)
# - Cookpots: two (4-player arena): the signature pot on the totem top (room for one banker) and one in the middle of
#   the left bridge (x 104): contested ground - heroes land there from the wrap ledge, the floor and over the totem,
#   and a stomp on a banker steals double. The seam, the only other mirror-symmetric place, cannot hold a pot (half
#   of it would be off the screen).
# - Spawns (rotate every round; 2 players use 1 and 2): 1 and 2 on the floor under the bridges by the totem (x 200 /
#   120, as at G1): a few steps from the big spot (a forward strike reaches col 9 from x 105 on the left and up to
#   x 198 on the right), and nothing lands on them from above. 3 and 4 on the outer ends of the bridges (x 72 / 248),
#   a drop above their own floor spots. A stomp is a landing (PHYSICS C.14 [G15]), so a hero pogoing under a bridge
#   is no longer robbed by whoever stands on it. (Tried: spawn 1 at x 184, 15 px inside the reach like spawn 2 -
#   Grub Stack evened out further, but Last Caveman Standing went to the edge of the +/-15 points.)
# - Modes: Grub Stack (default), Last Caveman Standing (sudden death: the stampede at 60 s) and Hot Rock; each has a
#   green bot set in core-B's tests/test_versus_bots.gd (12 seeds x 4 rounds, four Hunters).
# - Validator: clean (a run that ends at the totem's wall face is no gap).
# - Bot graph: resources/bots/arena_totem_ring.json, baked with core-B's tool after every edit of this file:
#   bash .tools/gd.sh script res://tools/bots/bake_nav.gd -- arena_totem_ring
# - Proof (G1): build/da/proof_totem_ring.gd (bash .tools/gd.sh script res://build/da/run_proof.gd -- --file=totem):
#   Grub Stack through Flow.start_versus, two humans on the classic one-keyboard layout (physical keys, NumLock on and
#   off) and two Rookie bots: the match finishes, no bot idles or misses a link at an empty head, no hit or stomp
#   lands on a hero whose spawn shield is up, each keyboard half drives only its hero, and the replay is identical.

[meta]
format = 2
id = arena_totem_ring
name = "Totem Ring"
kind = arena
biome = jungle
terrain_a = jungle/terrain_grass
terrain_b = ruins/terrain_carved
background = jungle
music = versus_battle_a
players = 4
modes = grub_stack,last_caveman,hot_rock
round_time = 90
wrap = lr
sudden = stampede
author = DA
notes = "Versus arena 1 (DESIGN.md E.5): jungle, wrap left-right, the cookpot on the totem top, springs to the wrap ledge, the big spot in the totem base (its giant onto the totem top), a second pot on the left bridge."

[legend]
? = objects/hidden_spot kind=small count=3 look=block tile=#
b = objects/hidden_spot kind=big look=inset tile=%
t = objects/hidden_spot kind=small count=3 look=block tile=%
J = objects/spring
P = objects/cookpot dx=8
Q = objects/cookpot
B = objects/spawn_point index=2
C = objects/spawn_point index=3
D = objects/spawn_point index=4

